    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2286; authority: candidate_only; category: 62; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;&lt;pattern&gt;WHAT IS A CATEGORY&lt;/pattern&gt;\n&lt;template&gt;&lt;br /&gt; AIML consists of a list of statements called categories.  Each&lt;br /&gt; category contains an input pattern and a reply template. &lt;br /&gt; The syntax of an AIML category is:&lt;br /&gt; &lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;category&amp;gt;&lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;pattern&amp;gt; PATTERN &amp;lt;/pattern&amp;gt;  &amp;lt;template&amp;gt; Template &amp;lt;/template&amp;gt;&lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;/category&amp;gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;br /&gt; or&lt;br /&gt; &lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;category&amp;gt;&lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;pattern&amp;gt; PATTERN &amp;lt;/pattern&amp;gt;&lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;that&amp;gt; THAT &amp;lt;/that&amp;gt;&lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;template&amp;gt; Template &amp;lt;/template&amp;gt;&lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;/category&amp;gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;br /&gt; The AIML category tags are case-sensitive.  Each open tag has an&lt;br /&gt; associated closing tag.  This syntax obviously derives from XML.&lt;br /&gt; &lt;br /&gt;&lt;/template&gt;\n&lt;/category&gt;\n; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁GENERAL_QA; id: 2286; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/ai.aiml#62; pattern: WHAT IS A CATEGORY; projection_order: 2279; source: data/alice/ai.aiml; source_hash: fb75dc36addf5da4b7ee2cacc24b4bb25c63405f1932ae315cfa0fbf095cb70b; template_kind: response; template_xml: &lt;br /&gt; AIML consists of a list of statements called categories.  Each AIML consists of a list of statements called categories.  Each&lt;br /&gt; category contains an input pattern and a reply template.  category contains an input pattern and a reply template. &lt;br /&gt; The syntax of an AIML category is: The syntax of an AIML category is:&lt;br /&gt;  &lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;category&amp;gt; &lt;category&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;pattern&amp;gt; PATTERN &amp;lt;/pattern&amp;gt;  &amp;lt;template&amp;gt; Template &amp;lt;/template&amp;gt; &lt;pattern&gt; PATTERN &lt;/pattern&gt;  &lt;template&gt; Template &lt;/template&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;/category&amp;gt; &lt;/category&gt;&lt;br /&gt;  &lt;br /&gt; or or&lt;br /&gt;  &lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;category&amp;gt; &lt;category&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;pattern&amp;gt; PATTERN &amp;lt;/pattern&amp;gt; &lt;pattern&gt; PATTERN &lt;/pattern&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;that&amp;gt; THAT &amp;lt;/that&amp;gt; &lt;that&gt; THAT &lt;/that&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;template&amp;gt; Template &amp;lt;/template&amp;gt; &lt;template&gt; Template &lt;/template&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &amp;lt;/category&amp;gt; &lt;/category&gt;&lt;br /&gt;  &lt;br /&gt; The AIML category tags are case-sensitive.  Each open tag has an The AIML category tags are case-sensitive.  Each open tag has an&lt;br /&gt; associated closing tag.  This syntax obviously derives from XML. associated closing tag.  This syntax obviously derives from XML.&lt;br /&gt;  &lt;br /&gt;; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
