    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2301; authority: candidate_only; category: 77; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;&lt;pattern&gt;WHAT IS XML&lt;/pattern&gt;\n&lt;template&gt;&lt;br /&gt; David Bacon pronounces it "Eggsmell".  XML is the Extensible&lt;br /&gt; Markup Language.  Like many "standards" in computer science, XML&lt;br /&gt; is a moving target.  In the simplest terms, XML is just a generalized&lt;br /&gt; version of HTML.  Anyone is free to define new XML tags, which&lt;br /&gt; look like HTML tags, and assign to them any meaning, within a context.&lt;br /&gt; AIML is an example of using the XML standard to define a specialized&lt;br /&gt; language for artificial intelligence.  &lt;br /&gt;    &lt;br /&gt; One reason to use an XML language is that there are numerous tools&lt;br /&gt; to edit and manipulate XML format files.  Another reason is that an&lt;br /&gt; XML language is easy for people to learn, if they are already&lt;br /&gt; familiar with HTML.  Third, AIML programs contain a mixture of&lt;br /&gt; AIML and HTML (and in principle other XML languages), a considerable &lt;br /&gt; convenience for programming web chat robots.&lt;br /&gt;    &lt;br /&gt; A good resource for information on XML is www.oasis-open.org.&lt;br /&gt;    &lt;br /&gt;&lt;/template&gt;\n&lt;/category&gt;\n; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁GENERAL_QA; id: 2301; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/ai.aiml#77; pattern: WHAT IS XML; projection_order: 2294; source: data/alice/ai.aiml; source_hash: fb75dc36addf5da4b7ee2cacc24b4bb25c63405f1932ae315cfa0fbf095cb70b; template_kind: response; template_xml: &lt;br /&gt; David Bacon pronounces it "Eggsmell".  XML is the Extensible David Bacon pronounces it "Eggsmell".  XML is the Extensible&lt;br /&gt; Markup Language.  Like many "standards" in computer science, XML Markup Language.  Like many "standards" in computer science, XML&lt;br /&gt; is a moving target.  In the simplest terms, XML is just a generalized is a moving target.  In the simplest terms, XML is just a generalized&lt;br /&gt; version of HTML.  Anyone is free to define new XML tags, which version of HTML.  Anyone is free to define new XML tags, which&lt;br /&gt; look like HTML tags, and assign to them any meaning, within a context. look like HTML tags, and assign to them any meaning, within a context.&lt;br /&gt; AIML is an example of using the XML standard to define a specialized AIML is an example of using the XML standard to define a specialized&lt;br /&gt; language for artificial intelligence.   language for artificial intelligence.  &lt;br /&gt;        &lt;br /&gt; One reason to use an XML language is that there are numerous tools One reason to use an XML language is that there are numerous tools&lt;br /&gt; to edit and manipulate XML format files.  Another reason is that an to edit and manipulate XML format files.  Another reason is that an&lt;br /&gt; XML language is easy for people to learn, if they are already XML language is easy for people to learn, if they are already&lt;br /&gt; familiar with HTML.  Third, AIML programs contain a mixture of familiar with HTML.  Third, AIML programs contain a mixture of&lt;br /&gt; AIML and HTML (and in principle other XML languages), a considerable  AIML and HTML (and in principle other XML languages), a considerable &lt;br /&gt; convenience for programming web chat robots. convenience for programming web chat robots.&lt;br /&gt;        &lt;br /&gt; A good resource for information on XML is www.oasis-open.org. A good resource for information on XML is www.oasis-open.org.&lt;br /&gt;        &lt;br /&gt;; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
