    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2504; authority: candidate_only; category: 17; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;HOW DOES A SEMANTIC GRAPH RELATE TO KNOWLEDGE REPRESENTATION&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;A semantic graph maps concepts to vertices and relationships to labelled edges. The adjacency list book(v) yields the manifest neighborhood: the set of concepts directly reachable from v in one hop.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2504; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#17; pattern: HOW DOES A SEMANTIC GRAPH RELATE TO KNOWLEDGE REPRESENTATION; projection_order: 2497; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: A semantic graph maps concepts to vertices and relationships to labelled edges. The adjacency list book(v) yields the manifest neighborhood: the set of concepts directly reachable from v in one hop.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
