    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2506; authority: candidate_only; category: 19; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;HOW DOES BFS DISTANCE DEFINE REACHABILITY IN A MICRONAUT NETWORK&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;BFS distance d(a,b) is the minimum number of edges traversed from a to b. delta_z(a,b) = 1/(1+d) maps distance to a [0,1] weight: adjacent nodes score near 1, unreachable nodes score 0.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n\n  \n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2506; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#19; pattern: HOW DOES BFS DISTANCE DEFINE REACHABILITY IN A MICRONAUT NETWORK; projection_order: 2499; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: BFS distance d(a,b) is the minimum number of edges traversed from a to b. delta_z(a,b) = 1/(1+d) maps distance to a [0,1] weight: adjacent nodes score near 1, unreachable nodes score 0.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
