    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2507; authority: candidate_only; category: 20; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;IS SPECTRAL CLUSTERING A RELIABLE METHOD FOR COMMUNITY DETECTION&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;Yes, under well-separated cluster assumptions. Spectral clustering uses the eigenvectors of the graph Laplacian to project vertices into a low-dimensional space before k-means clustering. It is robust to non-convex cluster shapes but sensitive to the choice of k.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2507; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#20; pattern: IS SPECTRAL CLUSTERING A RELIABLE METHOD FOR COMMUNITY DETECTION; projection_order: 2500; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: Yes, under well-separated cluster assumptions. Spectral clustering uses the eigenvectors of the graph Laplacian to project vertices into a low-dimensional space before k-means clustering. It is robust to non-convex cluster shapes but sensitive to the choice of k.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
