    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2526; authority: candidate_only; category: 39; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;WHAT IS A SEMANTIC FOLD IN KHANARY&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;A semantic fold is a topological operation recorded in fold_graph.xml that transitions the system between semantic phases. Each fold carries a source phase, an operation, a target phase, and a weight. Accumulated folds produce the ΔZ context that shapes the next Wo synthesis.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2526; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#39; pattern: WHAT IS A SEMANTIC FOLD IN KHANARY; projection_order: 2519; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: A semantic fold is a topological operation recorded in fold_graph.xml that transitions the system between semantic phases. Each fold carries a source phase, an operation, a target phase, and a weight. Accumulated folds produce the ΔZ context that shapes the next Wo synthesis.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE 2527</pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2527; authority: candidate_only; category: 40; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;HOW DOES FOLD GRAPH REPRESENT TOPOLOGICAL CHANGE&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;fold_graph.xml is the canonical fold specification. Each node encodes a phase transition (e.g. Pop→Yax) with an op label and weight. The incidence matrix B maps folds to phases; B*W_E*B^T produces the weighted fold-to-fold adjacency used by delta_z.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2527; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#40; pattern: HOW DOES FOLD GRAPH REPRESENT TOPOLOGICAL CHANGE; projection_order: 2520; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: fold_graph.xml is the canonical fold specification. Each node encodes a phase transition (e.g. Pop→Yax) with an op label and weight. The incidence matrix B maps folds to phases; B*W_E*B^T produces the weighted fold-to-fold adjacency used by delta_z.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
