    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2528; authority: candidate_only; category: 41; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;WHAT IS THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN A FOLD AND A RELATION&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;A fold is a phase-indexed operation on the topology — it changes what the system knows. A relation is a typed edge in G_semantic between two micronauts — it records a structural fact. Folds produce change; relations record it.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n\n  \n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2528; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#41; pattern: WHAT IS THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN A FOLD AND A RELATION; projection_order: 2521; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: A fold is a phase-indexed operation on the topology — it changes what the system knows. A relation is a typed edge in G_semantic between two micronauts — it records a structural fact. Folds produce change; relations record it.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
