    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2529; authority: candidate_only; category: 42; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;HOW DOES A FOLD RELATE TO A PHASE TRANSITION&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;Each fold entry in fold_graph.xml specifies a from_phase and to_phase. Executing a fold advances the system through the Pop→Wo→Yax→Sek→Ch'en→Xul cycle. The fold weight modulates how strongly the transition updates ΔZ.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2529; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#42; pattern: HOW DOES A FOLD RELATE TO A PHASE TRANSITION; projection_order: 2522; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: Each fold entry in fold_graph.xml specifies a from_phase and to_phase. Executing a fold advances the system through the Pop→Wo→Yax→Sek→Ch'en→Xul cycle. The fold weight modulates how strongly the transition updates ΔZ.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
