    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2530; authority: candidate_only; category: 43; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;WHAT IS THE RELATION BETWEEN FOLD LATTICE AND THE INCIDENCE MATRIX&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;The fold lattice is the algebraic structure induced by B (fold-phase incidence matrix). B*B^T gives fold-to-fold overlap; B^T*B gives phase-to-phase reachability via shared folds. The weighted version B*W_E*B^T is the topological score surface used in semantic_fold.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2530; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#43; pattern: WHAT IS THE RELATION BETWEEN FOLD LATTICE AND THE INCIDENCE MATRIX; projection_order: 2523; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: The fold lattice is the algebraic structure induced by B (fold-phase incidence matrix). B*B^T gives fold-to-fold overlap; B^T*B gives phase-to-phase reachability via shared folds. The weighted version B*W_E*B^T is the topological score surface used in semantic_fold.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE </pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2530; authority: candidate_only; category: 43; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;WHAT IS THE RELATION BETWEEN FOLD LATTICE AND THE INCIDENCE MATRIX&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;The fold lattice is the algebraic structure induced by B (fold-phase incidence matrix). B*B^T gives fold-to-fold overlap; B^T*B gives phase-to-phase reachability via shared folds. The weighted version B*W_E*B^T is the topological score surface used in semantic_fold.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2530; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#43; pattern: WHAT IS THE RELATION BETWEEN FOLD LATTICE AND THE INCIDENCE MATRIX; projection_order: 2523; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: The fold lattice is the algebraic structure induced by B (fold-phase incidence matrix). B*B^T gives fold-to-fold overlap; B^T*B gives phase-to-phase reachability via shared folds. The weighted version B*W_E*B^T is the topological score surface used in semantic_fold.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
