    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2531; authority: candidate_only; category: 44; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;HOW DOES DELTA Z MEASURE TOPOLOGICAL CHANGE IN THE SEMANTIC FOLD SURFACE&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;ΔZ = clamp01(W_µ · C_µ) after each scoring cycle. It captures the combined weight-confidence mass of the selected micronaut as a proxy for how much topology changed. High ΔZ means a confident, strongly-connected choice was made; near-zero means marginal selection.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n\n  \n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2531; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#44; pattern: HOW DOES DELTA Z MEASURE TOPOLOGICAL CHANGE IN THE SEMANTIC FOLD SURFACE; projection_order: 2524; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: ΔZ = clamp01(W_µ · C_µ) after each scoring cycle. It captures the combined weight-confidence mass of the selected micronaut as a proxy for how much topology changed. High ΔZ means a confident, strongly-connected choice was made; near-zero means marginal selection.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
