    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2532; authority: candidate_only; category: 45; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;IS THE FOLD KERNEL DETERMINISTIC UNDER THE SAME INPUT&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;Yes — the fold kernel is a pure function of its input token, phase context, and fold_graph weights. Given identical inputs and graph state it produces the same fold sequence. Non-determinism can only enter via stochastic model outputs upstream of the kernel.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2532; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#45; pattern: IS THE FOLD KERNEL DETERMINISTIC UNDER THE SAME INPUT; projection_order: 2525; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: Yes — the fold kernel is a pure function of its input token, phase context, and fold_graph weights. Given identical inputs and graph state it produces the same fold sequence. Non-determinism can only enter via stochastic model outputs upstream of the kernel.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
