    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2533; authority: candidate_only; category: 46; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;DOES THE FOLD GRAPH PRESERVE ORIENTATION UNDER SYMMETRIC FOLD&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;Yes for symmetric folds: if fold f maps phase A to phase B with weight w, the reverse is recorded as a separate fold entry from B to A. The orientation is explicit in the from_phase/to_phase fields, so symmetry is a design choice, not a structural guarantee.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n\n  \n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2533; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#46; pattern: DOES THE FOLD GRAPH PRESERVE ORIENTATION UNDER SYMMETRIC FOLD; projection_order: 2526; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: Yes for symmetric folds: if fold f maps phase A to phase B with weight w, the reverse is recorded as a separate fold entry from B to A. The orientation is explicit in the from_phase/to_phase fields, so symmetry is a design choice, not a structural guarantee.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
