  <category>
    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE 2552</pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2552; authority: candidate_only; category: 65; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;WHAT IS A PERCEPTION FIELD IN KHANARY&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;F_Q is an ephemeral 256-dimensional vector created at Pop phase by embed(query, confidence_context). It encodes the query direction in field space via sin-hash projection weighted 70% query / 30% context. It is L1-normalized and reset at Xul.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2552; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#65; pattern: WHAT IS A PERCEPTION FIELD IN KHANARY; projection_order: 2545; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: F_Q is an ephemeral 256-dimensional vector created at Pop phase by embed(query, confidence_context). It encodes the query direction in field space via sin-hash projection weighted 70% query / 30% context. It is L1-normalized and reset at Xul.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE </pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2552; authority: candidate_only; category: 65; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;WHAT IS A PERCEPTION FIELD IN KHANARY&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;F_Q is an ephemeral 256-dimensional vector created at Pop phase by embed(query, confidence_context). It encodes the query direction in field space via sin-hash projection weighted 70% query / 30% context. It is L1-normalized and reset at Xul.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2552; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#65; pattern: WHAT IS A PERCEPTION FIELD IN KHANARY; projection_order: 2545; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: F_Q is an ephemeral 256-dimensional vector created at Pop phase by embed(query, confidence_context). It encodes the query direction in field space via sin-hash projection weighted 70% query / 30% context. It is L1-normalized and reset at Xul.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE 2553</pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2553; authority: candidate_only; category: 66; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;HOW DOES F Q EMBED A QUERY INTO A FIELD VECTOR&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;embed() hashes the canonicalized query string, then for each dimension i computes sin((hash_byte * 0.1) + i) blended with the confidence_context[i]. The result is L1-normalized so the field lies on the probability simplex, making cosine comparisons stable.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2553; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#66; pattern: HOW DOES F Q EMBED A QUERY INTO A FIELD VECTOR; projection_order: 2546; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: embed() hashes the canonicalized query string, then for each dimension i computes sin((hash_byte * 0.1) + i) blended with the confidence_context[i]. The result is L1-normalized so the field lies on the probability simplex, making cosine comparisons stable.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE </pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2553; authority: candidate_only; category: 66; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;HOW DOES F Q EMBED A QUERY INTO A FIELD VECTOR&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;embed() hashes the canonicalized query string, then for each dimension i computes sin((hash_byte * 0.1) + i) blended with the confidence_context[i]. The result is L1-normalized so the field lies on the probability simplex, making cosine comparisons stable.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2553; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#66; pattern: HOW DOES F Q EMBED A QUERY INTO A FIELD VECTOR; projection_order: 2546; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: embed() hashes the canonicalized query string, then for each dimension i computes sin((hash_byte * 0.1) + i) blended with the confidence_context[i]. The result is L1-normalized so the field lies on the probability simplex, making cosine comparisons stable.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE 2554</pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2554; authority: candidate_only; category: 67; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;WHAT IS COSINE SIMILARITY IN THE CONTEXT OF SEMANTIC FIELDS&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;R_µ(Q) = clamp01((dot(F_Q, K_µ) / (|F_Q|·|K_µ|) + 1) / 2) where K_µ is the 256D sin-hash projection of the micronaut id. It measures directional alignment: 1.0 means perfect alignment, 0.5 is orthogonal, 0.0 is anti-aligned.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n\n  \n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2554; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#67; pattern: WHAT IS COSINE SIMILARITY IN THE CONTEXT OF SEMANTIC FIELDS; projection_order: 2547; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: R_µ(Q) = clamp01((dot(F_Q, K_µ) / (|F_Q|·|K_µ|) + 1) / 2) where K_µ is the 256D sin-hash projection of the micronaut id. It measures directional alignment: 1.0 means perfect alignment, 0.5 is orthogonal, 0.0 is anti-aligned.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE </pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2554; authority: candidate_only; category: 67; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;WHAT IS COSINE SIMILARITY IN THE CONTEXT OF SEMANTIC FIELDS&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;R_µ(Q) = clamp01((dot(F_Q, K_µ) / (|F_Q|·|K_µ|) + 1) / 2) where K_µ is the 256D sin-hash projection of the micronaut id. It measures directional alignment: 1.0 means perfect alignment, 0.5 is orthogonal, 0.0 is anti-aligned.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n\n  \n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2554; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#67; pattern: WHAT IS COSINE SIMILARITY IN THE CONTEXT OF SEMANTIC FIELDS; projection_order: 2547; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: R_µ(Q) = clamp01((dot(F_Q, K_µ) / (|F_Q|·|K_µ|) + 1) / 2) where K_µ is the 256D sin-hash projection of the micronaut id. It measures directional alignment: 1.0 means perfect alignment, 0.5 is orthogonal, 0.0 is anti-aligned.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE 2555</pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2555; authority: candidate_only; category: 68; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;HOW DOES A 3D FIELD VECTOR RELATE TO A 256 DIMENSIONAL PERCEPTION FIELD&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;The 3D refined_field_vec from a WCR delta is a directional hint from Gemma's question session. apply_wcr_delta() projects it to 256D via rx*sin(i*1.1)+ry*cos(i*0.9)+rz*sin(i*1.3+0.5), then blends into F_Q with alpha=delta_r. The 3D vector encodes semantic direction; the 256D field encodes query context.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2555; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#68; pattern: HOW DOES A 3D FIELD VECTOR RELATE TO A 256 DIMENSIONAL PERCEPTION FIELD; projection_order: 2548; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: The 3D refined_field_vec from a WCR delta is a directional hint from Gemma's question session. apply_wcr_delta() projects it to 256D via rx*sin(i*1.1)+ry*cos(i*0.9)+rz*sin(i*1.3+0.5), then blends into F_Q with alpha=delta_r. The 3D vector encodes semantic direction; the 256D field encodes query context.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE </pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2555; authority: candidate_only; category: 68; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;HOW DOES A 3D FIELD VECTOR RELATE TO A 256 DIMENSIONAL PERCEPTION FIELD&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;The 3D refined_field_vec from a WCR delta is a directional hint from Gemma's question session. apply_wcr_delta() projects it to 256D via rx*sin(i*1.1)+ry*cos(i*0.9)+rz*sin(i*1.3+0.5), then blends into F_Q with alpha=delta_r. The 3D vector encodes semantic direction; the 256D field encodes query context.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2555; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#68; pattern: HOW DOES A 3D FIELD VECTOR RELATE TO A 256 DIMENSIONAL PERCEPTION FIELD; projection_order: 2548; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: The 3D refined_field_vec from a WCR delta is a directional hint from Gemma's question session. apply_wcr_delta() projects it to 256D via rx*sin(i*1.1)+ry*cos(i*0.9)+rz*sin(i*1.3+0.5), then blends into F_Q with alpha=delta_r. The 3D vector encodes semantic direction; the 256D field encodes query context.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE 2556</pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2556; authority: candidate_only; category: 69; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;WHAT IS THE RELATION BETWEEN THE WCR SCORE AND THE SEMANTIC FIELD&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;S_µ(Q) = W_µ · C_µ · R_µ(Q). W comes from the semantic graph arc weights; C from ConfidenceStore; R from the cosine of F_Q against µ's hash projection. The field F_Q directly determines R, so shifting F_Q via ΔR nudges the ranking of all micronauts simultaneously.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2556; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#69; pattern: WHAT IS THE RELATION BETWEEN THE WCR SCORE AND THE SEMANTIC FIELD; projection_order: 2549; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: S_µ(Q) = W_µ · C_µ · R_µ(Q). W comes from the semantic graph arc weights; C from ConfidenceStore; R from the cosine of F_Q against µ's hash projection. The field F_Q directly determines R, so shifting F_Q via ΔR nudges the ranking of all micronauts simultaneously.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE </pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2556; authority: candidate_only; category: 69; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;WHAT IS THE RELATION BETWEEN THE WCR SCORE AND THE SEMANTIC FIELD&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;S_µ(Q) = W_µ · C_µ · R_µ(Q). W comes from the semantic graph arc weights; C from ConfidenceStore; R from the cosine of F_Q against µ's hash projection. The field F_Q directly determines R, so shifting F_Q via ΔR nudges the ranking of all micronauts simultaneously.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2556; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#69; pattern: WHAT IS THE RELATION BETWEEN THE WCR SCORE AND THE SEMANTIC FIELD; projection_order: 2549; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: S_µ(Q) = W_µ · C_µ · R_µ(Q). W comes from the semantic graph arc weights; C from ConfidenceStore; R from the cosine of F_Q against µ's hash projection. The field F_Q directly determines R, so shifting F_Q via ΔR nudges the ranking of all micronauts simultaneously.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE 2557</pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2557; authority: candidate_only; category: 70; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;HOW DOES DELTA R REFINE THE PERCEPTION FIELD TOWARD A MICRONAUT&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;apply_wcr_delta() blends a target vector T into F_Q: F_Q[i] = (1-alpha)*F_Q[i] + alpha*T[i], then L1-renormalizes. T is derived from refined_field_vec (Gemma's 3D hint) or falls back to the micronaut id hash. The blend alpha is capped at 0.15 per session.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n\n  \n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2557; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#70; pattern: HOW DOES DELTA R REFINE THE PERCEPTION FIELD TOWARD A MICRONAUT; projection_order: 2550; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: apply_wcr_delta() blends a target vector T into F_Q: F_Q[i] = (1-alpha)*F_Q[i] + alpha*T[i], then L1-renormalizes. T is derived from refined_field_vec (Gemma's 3D hint) or falls back to the micronaut id hash. The blend alpha is capped at 0.15 per session.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE </pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2557; authority: candidate_only; category: 70; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;HOW DOES DELTA R REFINE THE PERCEPTION FIELD TOWARD A MICRONAUT&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;apply_wcr_delta() blends a target vector T into F_Q: F_Q[i] = (1-alpha)*F_Q[i] + alpha*T[i], then L1-renormalizes. T is derived from refined_field_vec (Gemma's 3D hint) or falls back to the micronaut id hash. The blend alpha is capped at 0.15 per session.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n\n  \n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2557; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#70; pattern: HOW DOES DELTA R REFINE THE PERCEPTION FIELD TOWARD A MICRONAUT; projection_order: 2550; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: apply_wcr_delta() blends a target vector T into F_Q: F_Q[i] = (1-alpha)*F_Q[i] + alpha*T[i], then L1-renormalizes. T is derived from refined_field_vec (Gemma's 3D hint) or falls back to the micronaut id hash. The blend alpha is capped at 0.15 per session.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE 2558</pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2558; authority: candidate_only; category: 71; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;IS THE L1 NORMALIZED FIELD A VALID PROBABILITY DISTRIBUTION PROXY&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;Yes with caveats. L1 normalization ensures the field sums to 1 over its absolute values, which is necessary for a probability distribution over dimensions. However, the field contains negative values from sin projections, so it is a signed measure rather than a true probability distribution. The cosine similarity computation treats it as a direction vector regardless.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2558; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#71; pattern: IS THE L1 NORMALIZED FIELD A VALID PROBABILITY DISTRIBUTION PROXY; projection_order: 2551; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: Yes with caveats. L1 normalization ensures the field sums to 1 over its absolute values, which is necessary for a probability distribution over dimensions. However, the field contains negative values from sin projections, so it is a signed measure rather than a true probability distribution. The cosine similarity computation treats it as a direction vector regardless.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
  </category>
