    <pattern>GRAPH ELIZA-BIAS NODE 2559</pattern>
    <template>Graph eliza-bias; node 2559; authority: candidate_only; category: 72; category_xml: &lt;category&gt;\n    &lt;pattern&gt;DOES BLENDING REFINED FIELD VEC IMPROVE COSINE SIMILARITY WITH THE TARGET MICRONAUT&lt;/pattern&gt;\n    &lt;template&gt;Yes, when refined_field_vec is derived from Gemma's question answer about the micronaut. The blend moves F_Q toward the 256D direction of the micronaut id hash, increasing dot product and therefore R_µ(Q). The cap at alpha=0.15 prevents any single session from fully capturing the field.&lt;/template&gt;\n  &lt;/category&gt;\n\n  \n  ; default_bias: 1.0; field: ⟁KNOWLEDGE; id: 2559; kind: aiml_category; label: AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#72; pattern: DOES BLENDING REFINED FIELD VEC IMPROVE COSINE SIMILARITY WITH THE TARGET MICRONAUT; projection_order: 2552; source: data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml; source_hash: 690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78; template_kind: response; template_xml: Yes, when refined_field_vec is derived from Gemma's question answer about the micronaut. The blend moves F_Q toward the 256D direction of the micronaut id hash, increasing dot product and therefore R_µ(Q). The cap at alpha=0.15 prevents any single session from fully capturing the field.; wildcard_count: 0. Data-only graph record.</template>
